-- Migration: repair mojibake in notes from the February import
-- Created: 2026-08-18
--
-- The original CSV import read the file as Mac Roman instead of UTF-8, so every multi-byte
-- character in a note was stored as its bytes reinterpreted: ’ became ‚Äô, “ became ‚Äú, and
-- emoji became runs like \uf8ffüôè. Each statement re-encodes one note to Mac Roman bytes and
-- decodes them as UTF-8 — the exact inverse — with the result written out literally, so what
-- runs is what was reviewed.
--
-- 101 notes are repaired here. 1 more is corrupted but belongs to an entry that
-- still records no share type: migration 008's CHECK is NOT VALID, so it tolerates that row
-- but rejects any UPDATE to it. Repairing it means first deciding what was actually shared,
-- which no source records. It is left for a human.
--
-- Every UPDATE matches on the current (corrupted) text as well as the id, so a second run is
-- a no-op and a row edited in the meantime is left alone.
--
-- ROLLBACK: backups/notes-before-011-*.json holds every note as it was beforehand.

BEGIN;

UPDATE public.gospel_share_entries SET notes = $mojibake$Gospel response - My son, Bradley Atkinson

Multiple Spiritual Conversations with Bradley. He has had some health challenges and we talk about how God is still in control and He has a plan for Bradley’s life. Driving home from the hospital, we were talking about praying and being covered by prayer. I asked him to look up the Prayer of Salvation and tell me what it meant to him. We discussed his response and I asked him if he wanted say it with me and he said “yes”.

Bradley has said the prayer before with my wife (Tamara). This time (at 20 years old) he said he understood what he was saying and doing.

Please keep him covered in prayer and pray for us as we continue to disciple him.$mojibake$
  WHERE id = '1f8f036f-a021-445a-9715-c60edae74cc0' AND notes = $mojibake$Gospel response - My son, Bradley Atkinson

Multiple Spiritual Conversations with Bradley. He has had some health challenges and we talk about how God is still in control and He has a plan for Bradley‚Äôs life. Driving home from the hospital, we were talking about praying and being covered by prayer. I asked him to look up the Prayer of Salvation and tell me what it meant to him. We discussed his response and I asked him if he wanted say it with me and he said ‚Äúyes‚Äù.

Bradley has said the prayer before with my wife (Tamara). This time (at 20 years old) he said he understood what he was saying and doing.

Please keep him covered in prayer and pray for us as we continue to disciple him.$mojibake$;
UPDATE public.gospel_share_entries SET notes = $mojibake$During a conversation at the office, one young girl was telling that a family member had passed. 

She stopped and said, “he use to be really spiritual and went to church regularly but stopped many years back and had lived a sinful life since.” She stopped and asked,  “do you think he had time to make things right with God while he laid in the hospital dying.” 

That started a conversation with two of them one saying “I don’t know” and one saying “I don’t think so”.

 I asked them if I could tell them a story. 

I told them that The hardest part for believers is not having the ability to see into the hearts of the people around us, that only God can know that secret truth about us all. 

I then told them the story of the two thieves on the cross, and how that after a life of sin, it was their last words to God that determined their eternity.$mojibake$
  WHERE id = 'bc410371-822a-4bdf-b1cf-3b941545ad11' AND notes = $mojibake$During a conversation at the office, one young girl was telling that a family member had passed. 

She stopped and said, ‚Äúhe use to be really spiritual and went to church regularly but stopped many years back and had lived a sinful life since.‚Äù She stopped and asked,  ‚Äúdo you think he had time to make things right with God while he laid in the hospital dying.‚Äù 

That started a conversation with two of them one saying ‚ÄúI don‚Äôt know‚Äù and one saying ‚ÄúI don‚Äôt think so‚Äù.

 I asked them if I could tell them a story. 

I told them that The hardest part for believers is not having the ability to see into the hearts of the people around us, that only God can know that secret truth about us all. 

I then told them the story of the two thieves on the cross, and how that after a life of sin, it was their last words to God that determined their eternity.$mojibake$;
UPDATE public.gospel_share_entries SET notes = $mojibake$A co-worker was speaking withme and another co-worker and she expressed her fear in tithing.  I told her that there’s a verse for it but I couldn’t remember at the time. Fast forward about a week, during regroup, we spoke of Acts 5:1-11. I then realized that it was verse I wanted to speak on. The following day before leaving work that day I went to check on her because she wasn’t feeling good. I then brought up the scripture and shared that being honest with the Holy Spirit was the crime done.   This was so good opening to sharing more with each other.$mojibake$
  WHERE id = 'afb3e06a-36bc-49f7-8490-c7ae36018c68' AND notes = $mojibake$A co-worker was speaking withme and another co-worker and she expressed her fear in tithing.  I told her that there‚Äôs a verse for it but I couldn‚Äôt remember at the time. Fast forward about a week, during regroup, we spoke of Acts 5:1-11. I then realized that it was verse I wanted to speak on. The following day before leaving work that day I went to check on her because she wasn‚Äôt feeling good. I then brought up the scripture and shared that being honest with the Holy Spirit was the crime done.   This was so good opening to sharing more with each other.$mojibake$;
