UPDATE public.gospel_share_entries SET notes = $mojibake$ONE of the 33 people I shared the gospel with was with a close relative of mine. Our relationship was always rocky but got worse when our “Great Relative” died last year. After all the chaos that had happened within the last few weeks, i gathered the courage to tell them that I was sorry, I forgave them, and that I still loved them. But I also said that Jesus loved them more and that regardless of their past mistakes and choices in their lives, they are never far from His mercy and grace and love. I haven heard back from them and I’m not sure if I’ll ever speak to them again, but at least I know that I left them with the message of everlasting life, love, and peace, if they choose to take it.$mojibake$
  WHERE id = '48c639cf-f258-42cf-8461-43c59e4f3fa9' AND notes = $mojibake$ONE of the 33 people I shared the gospel with was with a close relative of mine. Our relationship was always rocky but got worse when our ‚ÄúGreat Relative‚Äù died last year. After all the chaos that had happened within the last few weeks, i gathered the courage to tell them that I was sorry, I forgave them, and that I still loved them. But I also said that Jesus loved them more and that regardless of their past mistakes and choices in their lives, they are never far from His mercy and grace and love. I haven heard back from them and I‚Äôm not sure if I‚Äôll ever speak to them again, but at least I know that I left them with the message of everlasting life, love, and peace, if they choose to take it.$mojibake$;
UPDATE public.gospel_share_entries SET notes = $mojibake$I’ve been reaching out/Praying for a former co-worker/friend Crystal. She was on the verge of visiting our Church, but a few months ago she started having two dialysis visits a week. She called me this week stating her legs sometimes feel heavy on the weekends, and that she will let me know when she’s able to attend. Please help me Pray for her healing. She’s also on the list to receive a Kidney. She’s professing Christianity, but the more I talk with her about her relationship with Christ I’m learning she’s been hurt, and not living for Christ to her potential.$mojibake$
  WHERE id = '80c3c627-5dbc-413a-84d9-f8ec69662b88' AND notes = $mojibake$I‚Äôve been reaching out/Praying for a former co-worker/friend Crystal. She was on the verge of visiting our Church, but a few months ago she started having two dialysis visits a week. She called me this week stating her legs sometimes feel heavy on the weekends, and that she will let me know when she‚Äôs able to attend. Please help me Pray for her healing. She‚Äôs also on the list to receive a Kidney. She‚Äôs professing Christianity, but the more I talk with her about her relationship with Christ I‚Äôm learning she‚Äôs been hurt, and not living for Christ to her potential.$mojibake$;
UPDATE public.gospel_share_entries SET notes = $mojibake$A friend recently lost her Father to Cancer, and shared he was a Christian, and she was grateful for that. I Prayed with her a couple of times, and we have had great conversations of the goodness of God. She has two sons. One recently gave his life to the Lord. I asked her was her 17 year old that lives with his dad in VA a Christian, and did she lead him to the Lord. She stated no, so I immediately encouraged her to call him to have a conversation about her story, and introduce God to him. She stated thru the years she’s had conversations about Jesus, but hasn’t led him to the Lord. She’s dealt with major behavioral problems with him for several years, so he had to go live with his dad. Please help Pray for Jamir that his heart will be open to receive the Lord as his Savior. Thank You!!$mojibake$
  WHERE id = '1fd592cc-8858-44cd-ad64-74dfec9df2da' AND notes = $mojibake$A friend recently lost her Father to Cancer, and shared he was a Christian, and she was grateful for that. I Prayed with her a couple of times, and we have had great conversations of the goodness of God. She has two sons. One recently gave his life to the Lord. I asked her was her 17 year old that lives with his dad in VA a Christian, and did she lead him to the Lord. She stated no, so I immediately encouraged her to call him to have a conversation about her story, and introduce God to him. She stated thru the years she‚Äôs had conversations about Jesus, but hasn‚Äôt led him to the Lord. She‚Äôs dealt with major behavioral problems with him for several years, so he had to go live with his dad. Please help Pray for Jamir that his heart will be open to receive the Lord as his Savior. Thank You!!$mojibake$;
UPDATE public.gospel_share_entries SET notes = $mojibake$I didn’t realize that I would have a similar story as I did the week before. I’ve been having conversations with another friend Kelly concerning her son Coby going thru heart problems at 21 yrs old up until a recent successful surgery, and consistently in Prayer for him. I didn’t want to assume he was a Christian as she, so I asked the question as I asked my Friend Kadia about her son, is Coby a Christian. She pause, and said, I’m working on that. She knows how important it is that the Lord becomes his Savior. I’m reminded all the time that we can’t look at someone, or their Family dynamics & assume they have a personal relationship with our Father. Kelly told me he went to Church with her last Sunday, and she was happy for that. I desire Prayers for Coby’s Health, and Salvation. Thank You!$mojibake$
  WHERE id = 'b9b8f4da-4d66-467d-bbf1-0f0c1b6e92c2' AND notes = $mojibake$I didn‚Äôt realize that I would have a similar story as I did the week before. I‚Äôve been having conversations with another friend Kelly concerning her son Coby going thru heart problems at 21 yrs old up until a recent successful surgery, and consistently in Prayer for him. I didn‚Äôt want to assume he was a Christian as she, so I asked the question as I asked my Friend Kadia about her son, is Coby a Christian. She pause, and said, I‚Äôm working on that. She knows how important it is that the Lord becomes his Savior. I‚Äôm reminded all the time that we can‚Äôt look at someone, or their Family dynamics & assume they have a personal relationship with our Father. Kelly told me he went to Church with her last Sunday, and she was happy for that. I desire Prayers for Coby‚Äôs Health, and Salvation. Thank You!$mojibake$;
