UPDATE public.gospel_share_entries SET notes = $mojibake$Responded to a comment on Youtube. The person mentioned how many Christians can’t get closer to God due to the type of relationship they had/have with their earthly father. I agreed with that person’s comment and let them know that for years, that was me but that God had revealed to me that He was my True Father and that I was viewing Him through the hurt, pain, disappointment, judgement, lack of compassion, intimacy, and tenderness, I had experienced with my earthly father. He told me that He is nothing like my earthly father. From that moment on, the veil was lifted and the scales removed. I no longer felt rejected or that I was missing out, especially, father/daughter relationship. That void was filled by the unconditional and perfect love of my Father, Almighty God. And later, during online Bible Study, the Pastor leading it mentioned that God is our Father and that He had just used our earthly father to get us here.$mojibake$
  WHERE id = 'a65386c7-054c-470f-af87-b0ab45c96245' AND notes = $mojibake$Responded to a comment on Youtube. The person mentioned how many Christians can‚Äôt get closer to God due to the type of relationship they had/have with their earthly father. I agreed with that person‚Äôs comment and let them know that for years, that was me but that God had revealed to me that He was my True Father and that I was viewing Him through the hurt, pain, disappointment, judgement, lack of compassion, intimacy, and tenderness, I had experienced with my earthly father. He told me that He is nothing like my earthly father. From that moment on, the veil was lifted and the scales removed. I no longer felt rejected or that I was missing out, especially, father/daughter relationship. That void was filled by the unconditional and perfect love of my Father, Almighty God. And later, during online Bible Study, the Pastor leading it mentioned that God is our Father and that He had just used our earthly father to get us here.$mojibake$;
UPDATE public.gospel_share_entries SET notes = $mojibake$Last night, Isaiah and I, was able to share the love of God  with a young lady by the name of Rebbeca, in the McDonald’s parking lot (632 Memorial Dr). We saw her walking from car to car asking for change. When she got to my car, I told her that I only had a debit card and would love to feed her if she is hungry. She agreed and told me what she wanted. Before making another trip to the drive through, we handed her a couple bottled waters, hand sanitizer, hand cream, and an unopened chapstick from my purse. I told her to wait in front of the restaurant and we would go get her food and meet her there. We ended up getting her a Mc Donald’s gift card instead of the food. I pulled around to the front of the restaurant and notion for her to follow me to a parking spot. While parked, we talked a little and then I began to remind her of God’s love and that we can never fall too far from God’s grace. I told her that she matters to God and that our tears are prayers. God sees, hears, and understands them. He hears both our heart’s cries and desires. I let her know that what she is going through is temporary and that it will not always be like this. My heart wanted to just embrace her and tell her to get in my car and take her home. Common sense and wisdom of course said, no…not the smartest thing to do. Lastly, I told her that we would remember her and to keep her lifted ip in prayer. I have to say, her eyes stood out to me. They were a beautiful gray. The white part of her eyes were free of broken vessels and discoloration. Just pure white. And all I kept thinking is, Almighty God gave her those beautiful eyes. It reminded me that she too was fearfully and wonderfully made. I wish I had told her that. Maybe she already knew and/or it wasn’t something that the Holy Spirit intended for me to say? Even now as I type this, I can see her lovely eyes.$mojibake$
  WHERE id = '479d9243-0f5e-4dbd-acee-beeee91d1189' AND notes = $mojibake$Last night, Isaiah and I, was able to share the love of God  with a young lady by the name of Rebbeca, in the McDonald‚Äôs parking lot (632 Memorial Dr). We saw her walking from car to car asking for change. When she got to my car, I told her that I only had a debit card and would love to feed her if she is hungry. She agreed and told me what she wanted. Before making another trip to the drive through, we handed her a couple bottled waters, hand sanitizer, hand cream, and an unopened chapstick from my purse. I told her to wait in front of the restaurant and we would go get her food and meet her there. We ended up getting her a Mc Donald‚Äôs gift card instead of the food. I pulled around to the front of the restaurant and notion for her to follow me to a parking spot. While parked, we talked a little and then I began to remind her of God‚Äôs love and that we can never fall too far from God‚Äôs grace. I told her that she matters to God and that our tears are prayers. God sees, hears, and understands them. He hears both our heart‚Äôs cries and desires. I let her know that what she is going through is temporary and that it will not always be like this. My heart wanted to just embrace her and tell her to get in my car and take her home. Common sense and wisdom of course said, no‚Ä¶not the smartest thing to do. Lastly, I told her that we would remember her and to keep her lifted ip in prayer. I have to say, her eyes stood out to me. They were a beautiful gray. The white part of her eyes were free of broken vessels and discoloration. Just pure white. And all I kept thinking is, Almighty God gave her those beautiful eyes. It reminded me that she too was fearfully and wonderfully made. I wish I had told her that. Maybe she already knew and/or it wasn‚Äôt something that the Holy Spirit intended for me to say? Even now as I type this, I can see her lovely eyes.$mojibake$;
