I asked her if she needed a prayer for anything and she said she needed prayer for a car and that she would just be kept safe in it once she gets one. So I prayed for her and then I got in my car.  The Holy Spirit say you need to go back and ask her if she wants to come to Reimage Church for a visit.

She just moved to here recently and her grandmother has a church she goes to, but it‚Äôs in Bridgeton, which is far for her and since she doesn‚Äôt have a car so I gave her my name and number to let her know that she could call me$mojibake$;
UPDATE public.gospel_share_entries SET notes = $mojibake$A group of us from DMD were at the mall to disciple, tell Gods story or pray for people. After being there for an hour we found out the mall closed at 7. 

Just before we were about to leave, A young lady approached us and asked if we had jumper cables Because her car wouldn’t start. Pastor Chris went out to help her and then maybe 10 minutes later we follow to check on him and the young lady.

Once the car started, I opened the passenger side door to see if she was ok. With tears in her eyes she thanked us. I obeyed the Holy Spirit and sat down in the passenger seat and talked to her a little bit and gave her a little of my story and asked her to tell me a little bit about her and she told me some things and we prayed. she said she knew Jesus and she had just gotten away from him for a while. I gave her my telephone number. I told her about Reimage Church. I asked her to text me when she got home OK and she did and then asked me about the name of our church and the number and I gave it to her.

I plan on reaching out to her sometime this weekend. It was amazing to see God at work!$mojibake$
